  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_027 (multimodal, pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.535 acc, a modest +5pt gain over RNA-only (0.485), while image alone is very weak (0.227). This suggests the image signal is noisy and its contribution may be suboptimal under simple concatenation. Question: Does weighted fusion (config_032) improve over concat by appropriately downweighting the weak image modality? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_027—only the fusion method changes. Why best next: Under a limited budget, isolating the fusion mechanism is the highest-information experiment because it directly informs whether the image modality's value is being properly extracted. If weighted > concat, it confirms the image adds useful but noisy signal and guides all future multimodal designs; if equal, concat suffices and we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or multiprofile questions. No other single experiment reduces uncertainty about this critical design axis as efficiently."
}

